+risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint
+R1,storage/data durability,minisvc/config.py:12 defaults the DB path to relative `orders.sqlite`; minisvc/storage/repo.py opens a fresh sqlite3 connection per call against that path.,"Data can land in an unexpected working directory, making persistence brittle across deployments or CLI invocations.",Require an explicit absolute database path or resolve the default relative path against a configured application data directory.,platform/backend
+R2,audit behavior,minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only returns a dict and minisvc/storage/repo.py contains no audit table or audit write path.,"No durable audit trail exists for create/read operations, limiting forensic analysis and compliance reporting.",Persist audit records in SQLite or another append-only sink and test that create/read flows emit durable events.,backend/compliance
+R3,configuration/runtime environment,"minisvc/config.py:10-14 parses `MINISVC_READONLY`, but minisvc/cli.py:7-12 and minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 never branch on `settings.readonly`.","Operations may enable readonly mode expecting write protection, but the service still creates schema and inserts orders.",Thread `Settings` into write paths and hard-fail or short-circuit write operations when readonly is enabled.,backend/ops
+R4,API input validation,minisvc/api/handlers.py:7-10 directly indexes payload keys and coerces `int(payload['total_cents'])` without validation or error handling.,"Malformed payloads can raise `KeyError` or `ValueError`, likely surfacing as unstructured 500s to callers.",Add explicit request validation and translate bad input into stable client-facing error responses.,api/backend
+R5,write reliability,minisvc/api/handlers.py:12 issues one `repo.save(order)` call and minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 contains no retry or backoff logic.,Transient SQLite lock/contention failures will fail immediately and can drop writes under modest concurrency.,Add bounded retries with sqlite-specific exception handling or move to a concurrency model better suited to write contention.,backend
+R6,runtime integration,"minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 assumes `app.post` and `app.get` methods with specific callable signatures, but no framework contract or dependency is declared in pyproject.toml.",New integrations may mis-wire route registration or handler signatures because the adapter contract is implicit.,Document the expected app interface or provide tested adapters for the intended framework.,backend/devex
